// Brave Search REST: the `brave` provider of the web_search chain.
//
// Wire contract pinned from Brave's own Web Search API documentation (read
// 2026-10-20):
// - API reference, https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/api-reference/web/search/get
//   (base URL https://api.search.brave.com/res, operation GET /v1/web/search);
// - authentication guide, https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/guides/authentication;
// - rate-limiting guide, https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/guides/rate-limiting;
// - search operators guide, https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/resources/search-operators.
//
// - method and path: GET /res/v1/web/search on https://api.search.brave.com,
//   with every argument in the query string;
// - auth: "All requests to the Brave Search API must include an API key in the
//   X-Subscription-Token HTTP header", the raw key with no prefix. The
//   connection is bound to the vault credential `apikey:brave`; plexus reads it
//   by name at dispatch and never stores it. The key never travels in the URL;
// - request fields: `q` (required; "Maximum of 600 characters and 75 words"),
//   `count` (1 to 20, default 20), `freshness` (`pd`, `pw`, `pm`, `py`: 24
//   hours, 7 days, 31 days, 365 days), `extra_snippets` ("up to 5 additional,
//   alternative excerpts") and `text_decorations` (default true: "decoration
//   markers (e.g. highlighting characters)" in display strings; sent as false);
// - domains: Brave has no domain parameter. Domains go into `q` as `site:`
//   operators joined by uppercase `OR`, the form the operator guide shows
//   ("electric vehicles site:reuters.com OR site:bloomberg.com 2025"). The
//   guide documents no grouping with parentheses, so none is sent;
// - reply: `web` is optional ("Web results relevant to the query"); its
//   `results[]` items carry `title`, `url`, `description`, `extra_snippets`,
//   `age` ("A human-readable representation of the web search result's age.
//   For example, `2 days ago`") and `page_age` ("The page's date, based on its
//   published or last modified date");
// - documented errors: 404, 422 and 429, each with an `error` object carrying
//   `id`, `status`, `code`, `detail` and `meta`. Exceeding a rate limit is a
//   429. The plan's monthly quota is one of those rate-limit windows
//   (X-RateLimit-Limit "1, 15000": per second and per month), so a used-up
//   monthly quota is also a 429. No Retry-After header is documented, only
//   X-RateLimit-Reset.
//
// Differences from the provider facts the web_search chain design started from
// (X-Subscription-Token; q, count up to 20 and freshness; domains via query
// operators; query at most 500 characters; web.results[].title, url,
// description plus extra_snippets, and age):
// - Brave documents 600 characters, not 500. BraveRestBackend keeps the
//   500-character limit, which is the tool's own query limit, and checks it
//   on the final `q` after the site: operators are added. It also enforces
//   Brave's 75-word limit on that final string; a longer query skips Brave as
//   a capability mismatch rather than being sent;
// - `age` is relative text in most replies. The publication date comes from
//   `page_age` when present, and from `age` only when that is an absolute
//   date; a relative age such as "2 days ago" is dropped, not guessed;
// - every request also sends `text_decorations=false`, so titles and
//   descriptions arrive without highlighting markup;
// - a missing or invalid key: Brave's reference documents no 401. Clients
//   that call the live API report an invalid key as HTTP 422 with
//   error.code SUBSCRIPTION_TOKEN_INVALID (for example
//   kennbroorg/iKy backend/factories/search_providers.py and
//   perminder-klair/subwave controller/src/routes/settings/llm.ts, the
//   latter "verified live"). web_search classifies every 400 and 422 as a
//   rejected request without reading the body, so with a wrong key every
//   ordered search stops at Brave with web_search_request_rejected: no
//   cooldown and no fallthrough to the next provider. The rollout's live
//   check sends a real Brave search with the stored key to catch this
//   before an order containing brave is set;
// - a used-up monthly quota is a 429 like any rate limit, so web_search
//   treats it as throttled: a 60-second cooldown (no Retry-After is
//   documented), not the one-hour quota cooldown.
//
// The search action is read-risk and has no side effects, so a retry is safe.
// No other Brave endpoint is declared: web_search needs only web search.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "key": "brave_rest",
  "name": "Brave Search (REST)",
  "description": "Web search over Brave's Search API, as a provider for web_search.",
  "reuse_path": "openapi_shim",
  "reuse_rationale": "Documented REST API with a published reference and a static API-key header; search mutates no vendor-side state, so it maps to a read grant.",
  "tier": "S1",
  "transport": {
    "kind": "rest_api",
    "url": "https://api.search.brave.com"
  },
  "auth": {
    "mode": "api_key"
  },
  "credential_bindings": [
    {
      "ref_role": "api_key",
      "placement": "header",
      "key": "X-Subscription-Token",
      "prefix": "",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "resource_filters": {
    "required": [],
    "optional": [],
    "write_enabling": []
  },
  "actions_baseline": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "risk": "read",
      "http": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/res/v1/web/search",
        "parameters": "query",
        "args_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "q": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 600 },
            "count": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20 },
            "freshness": { "type": "string", "enum": ["pd", "pw", "pm", "py"] },
            "extra_snippets": { "type": "boolean" },
            "text_decorations": { "type": "boolean" }
          },
          "required": ["q"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "ask_first_risk": ["write", "destructive"],
    "rate_limit": { "calls_per_min": 30 }
  },
  "availability": "ga"
}
